# PR #1324 review comment — cdz-kernel/src/kernel.rs (v-agent-harness)

Mirrored from https://github.com/camshaft/cadenza/pull/1324 (PR: "cand: v-agent-harness — a6db0d731").

## Report-query test claims "no effects" but never asserts the fork executor was unused (Copilot, kernel.rs:1297) — test-coverage
> The test comment claims the report-based query performs no effects ("RecordingExecutor saw no
> effects"), but it never asserts that the fork executor was unused. Without an assertion, a
> regression that accidentally dispatches effects during a `report` query could slip through.

Add the missing assertion (e.g. the RecordingExecutor's captured-effects count is 0 / the fork
executor was never invoked) so the "report performs no effects" invariant is actually pinned rather
than just asserted in prose.
